{"agent":"fleet-fixes-p","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The change adds `.gitattributes` to the set that `_record_written` marks as written by `pins regenerate`, and the accompanying test makes the new semantics explicit: after regenerate writes the `merge=pinsregen` line, `git add .gitattributes` then `_verdict(repo)` must return `OK` with no lease anywhere in the test (`tests/test_pins_output_commit.py:122-127`). The recorded authorization model limits auto-allow to files inside the worktree and lease-covered repo files [D-acp-r2]; a repo-root `.gitattributes` in the primary repository is neither, yet this change makes it committable with no lease. That matters more than for the pin files the exemption was written for: `.gitattributes` is repo-wide merge behaviour (`merge=`, filter and text attributes apply to every path), so once a regenerate has touched it, its content can be committed through the same path without the lease/approval gate that the decision says every state-changing action must still pass. A concrete instance is exactly the new test's setup (primary repo, run `pins regenerate`, `git add .gitattributes`, commit succeeds without a lease) — if the intended rule is \"pins are never leased\" only for generated pin outputs, `.gitattributes` needs either to be a lease-covered repo file or to be excluded from the never-lease set.","digest":"3993a56eebdf5d8d","location":"ddflow/api/pin_files.py:49 (`watched = [*files, \".gitattributes\"]`)","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/api/pin_files.py:49 (`watched = [*files, \".gitattributes\"]`)"}],"chunks_total":1,"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":3003,"diff_sha":"2dbbe8c8867b33973d4cd2eb3b40130face2443c39912aa6f99c7cd9b9e87fd9","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":107.4,"family":"deepseek","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","output_digest":"d2b46a4028a289fb","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/DX-pins-gitattributes-dirty.rubber_duck.lan-deepseek-v4.1-flash.20261018T014416Z-b43d9e83.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1],"reviewed_head":"0a2927d3aedd9a9336993981dd0b769d865e7c13","reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewer_digest":"d34b8af1b4a590b5","round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/api/pin_files.py:49 (`watched = [*files, \".gitattributes\"]`)"],"tree_sha":"0a2927d3aedd+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":"1 finding(s)"},"id":"e65af2efafcfbd141eb9d0f0a","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":77958,"schema":1,"subject":"DX-pins-gitattributes-dirty","ts":"2026-10-18T01:46:03.716385Z"}
